{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792571589530,"sessionID":"ses_ea2691a44ffemHBxOiocBq67ci","part":{"partID":"prt_15d97c392001qjW6LA96e3sdDE","sessionID":"ses_ea2691a44ffemHBxOiocBq67ci","messageID":"msg_15d97b732001h55p64rDZWShhh","type":"tool","id":"call_02_a24lstnpdqmafjzkvs0zq9gq","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/AUTHOR_INPUT.json"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/AUTHOR_INPUT.json, lines 1-162\n1: {\n2:  \"name\": \"Home Care Ledger\",\n3:  \"audience\": \"A single homeowner keeping care records for their own home on a local machine, with no accounts, notifications, or multi-property operation.\",\n4:  \"objective\": \"Create the home and its equipment, define every-N-day care plans anchored to them, see exactly which tasks are due or overdue as of a date, record a completion with a note, advance the next due date from the actual completion date, and retrieve care history by home or equipment.\",\n5:  \"workflow\": [\n6:   \"Start the local server against a disposable data directory; initialize the SQLite schema on first start.\",\n7:   \"Create the single home with POST /api/home, then add equipment records with POST /api/equipment anchored by home_id.\",\n8:   \"Create care plans with POST /api/plans using interval_days and an optional equipment anchor.\",\n9:   \"Query GET /api/tasks/due with an explicit as_of and horizon_days to see overdue, due, and upcoming work.\",\n10:   \"Record a completion and note with POST /api/plans/{id}/completions; the same transaction updates the plan next due date.\",\n11:   \"Read GET /api/plans/{id}/completions or GET /api/history filtered by home_id and equipment_id.\",\n12:   \"Use GET / for the basic accessible single-page UI; all actions remain available through the documented JSON API.\"\n13:  ],\n14:  \"acceptance\": [\n15:   \"A fresh database has no home; POST /api/home creates exactly one record with id home, and a second POST returns 409 HOME_EXISTS without mutating the stored home.\",\n16:   \"POST /api/equipment under the existing home returns 201 and round-trips through list and detail; blank names, invalid categories, and unknown homes return 422 or 404 and add no equipment row.\",\n17:   \"POST /api/plans enforces interval_days 1..3650 and mutual exclusion of last_completed_on and first_due_on; GET /api/tasks/due returns exact overdue, due, and upcoming sets at as_of and horizon_days boundaries, while invalid requests write nothing.\",\n18:   \"A completion with note inserts one history row and atomically sets due_on to max(previous last_completed_on, completed_on) plus interval_days; leap-day, month-end, year-end, future-date, oversize-note, and unknown-plan failures leave both plan and completions unchanged.\",\n19:   \"GET /api/history filters by home and equipment and returns documented fields in descending completion order; invalid filters write nothing; GET / is dependency-free accessible HTML and unknown routes or methods return documented JSON errors.\"\n20:  ],\n21:  \"observations\": [\n22:   [\n23:    \"documentation\",\n24:    \"README.md\",\n25:    17,\n26:    17,\n27:    \"Document claim: micasa describes itself as home maintenance from the terminal, a local tool rather than a hosted multi-tenant service.\"\n28:   ],\n29:   [\n30:    \"documentation\",\n31:    \"README.md\",\n32:    25,\n33:    25,\n34:    \"Document claim: the upstream advertises schedules, due dates, and full history.\"\n35:   ],\n36:   [\n37:    \"code_observation\",\n38:    \"internal/data/models.go\",\n39:    104,\n40:    135,\n41:    \"Code observation: HouseProfile stores address, year built, systems, and other attributes; no explicit multi-home ownership table is observed in the selected files.\"\n42:   ],\n43:   [\n44:    \"code_observation\",\n45:    \"internal/data/models.go\",\n46:    201,\n47:    216,\n48:    \"Code observation: Appliance stores make, model, serial, warranty, and location, with no home_id field observed.\"\n49:   ],\n50:   [\n51:    \"code_observation\",\n52:    \"internal/data/models.go\",\n53:    218,\n54:    237,\n55:    \"Code observation: MaintenanceItem has an optional ApplianceID, category, season, interval months, last serviced date, and due date.\"\n56:   ],\n57:   [\n58:    \"code_observation\",\n59:    \"internal/data/models.go\",\n60:    261,\n61:    274,\n62:    \"Code observation: ServiceLogEntry belongs to a maintenance item and stores serviced_at, optional vendor and cost, notes, and timestamps.\"\n63:   ],\n64:   [\n65:    \"code_observation\",\n66:    \"internal/data/store_house.go\",\n67:    22,\n68:    31,\n69:    \"Code observation: CreateHouseProfile counts existing profiles and rejects a second row, implementing one house profile.\"\n70:   ],\n71:   [\n72:    \"code_observation\",\n73:    \"internal/data/store_maintenance.go\",\n74:    24,\n75:    33,\n76:    \"Code observation: ListMaintenanceByAppliance filters maintenance items by appliance id, showing an equipment-anchored query path.\"\n77:   ],\n78:   [\n79:    \"code_observation\",\n80:    \"internal/data/store_servicelog.go\",\n81:    16,\n82:    30,\n83:    \"Code observation: syncLastServiced sets LastServicedAt to the most recent non-deleted serviced_at.\"\n84:   ],\n85:   [\n86:    \"code_observation\",\n87:    \"internal/data/store_servicelog.go\",\n88:    59,\n89:    73,\n90:    \"Code observation: CreateServiceLog runs in a transaction, creates the service log, then syncs the parent maintenance item.\"\n91:   ],\n92:   [\n93:    \"code_observation\",\n94:    \"internal/data/validation.go\",\n95:    168,\n96:    177,\n97:    \"Code observation: ComputeNextDue returns an explicit due date when set, otherwise adds interval months to the last service date.\"\n98:   ],\n99:   [\n100:    \"code_observation\",\n101:    \"internal/data/validation.go\",\n102:    182,\n103:    192,\n104:    \"Code observation: AddMonths clamps the day to the target month end, avoiding the Jan 31 plus one month overflow.\"\n105:   ],\n106:   [\n107:    \"code_observation\",\n108:    \"internal/data/validation.go\",\n109:    98,\n110:    153,\n111:    \"Code observation: interval parsing accepts years and months, not days.\"\n112:   ],\n113:   [\n114:    \"code_observation\",\n115:    \"internal/data/dashboard.go\",\n116:    12,\n117:    25,\n118:    \"Code observation: scheduled maintenance is defined as interval months greater than zero or an explicit due date.\"\n119:   ],\n120:   [\n121:    \"documentation\",\n122:    \"README.md\",\n123:    58,\n124:    58,\n125:    \"Document claim: the upstream is pure Go using SQLite and a terminal UI; this target does not copy or run that implementation.\"\n126:   ]\n127:  ],\n128:  \"inference\": \"Target design inference, not an upstream claim: the pinned research makes the home the subject and requires recurring work plus a durable completion record. Upstream code corroborates that abstract shape but realizes recurrence in months, keeps one house profile, links maintenance to an optional appliance, and does not show an explicit appliance-to-home foreign key in the selected files. The target therefore makes the home anchor explicit through home_id on equipment and plans, uses every-N-days recurrence from the scenario, and keeps only the home, equipment, plan, completion, and history slice. It does not copy upstream code, schema, or UI. Upstream status: not_run; no upstream build, test, server, TUI, or database was started.\",\n129:  \"features\": [\n130:   \"Home and equipment anchor\",\n131:   \"Every-N-day plan and due queue\",\n132:   \"Completion and next-due rollover\",\n133:   \"Anchored care history\",\n134:   \"Accessible localhost UI\"\n135:  ],\n136:  \"goals\": [\n137:   \"In a dedicated data directory, create the single home, add an equipment record under it, and prove duplicate-home and invalid-equipment requests return 409, 422, or 404 without changing stored records.\",\n138:   \"Create plans with interval_days in 1..3650 and verify GET /api/tasks/due returns the exact overdue, due, and upcoming sets at the as_of and horizon_days boundaries while invalid plans write nothing.\",\n139:   \"Record a completion and note in one atomic call and verify due_on becomes max(previous last_completed_on, completed_on) plus interval_days across leap-day, month-end, and year-end examples, with invalid completions leaving no trace.\",\n140:   \"Retrieve completions filtered by home and equipment in documented descending order with plan and equipment names and notes, and reject invalid filters without writes.\",\n141:   \"Load GET / and assert a dependency-free, labelled, keyboard-accessible HTML shell exposes home, equipment, plan, due, completion, and history workflows, while unknown routes and methods return documented JSON errors.\"\n142:  ],\n143:  \"arch\": \"# Home Care Ledger: target architecture\\n\\n## Scope and decisions to confirm\\n- Local single-user target: one homeowner, one home, loopback only.\\n- Python 3.11+ standard library only; SQLite; no third-party packages.\\n- This is a cognition template, not an application and not the upstream micasa codebase.\\n- Deliberately excluded: accounts and authentication, notifications, email, vendors, costs, quotes, projects, documents, manuals, photos, payments, LLM, multi-property, imports and exports, and deletion endpoints.\\n- Decision: exactly one home with fixed id `home`, because the pinned scenario is the user's own home and upstream exposes a single house profile.\\n- Decision: recurrence is every N calendar days, 1..3650, because the scenario says every N days. Upstream uses interval months; this target is not API-compatible with it.\\n- Decision: a plan created without an anchor is due on the server local creation date.\\n- Decision: a backdated completion never moves next due backwards; next due is based on the latest completion date.\\n- Decision: no natural-language dates and no timezone-bearing timestamps in domain dates.\\n\\n## Runtime, data directory, start\\n- Source file `app.py`; database `$HOMECARE_DATA_DIR/homecare.sqlite3`.\\n- `HOMECARE_DATA_DIR` defaults to `./data`; the directory is created if absent.\\n- Start: `python3 app.py --data-dir ./data --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765`.\\n- Equivalent environment variables: `HOMECARE_DATA_DIR`, `HOMECARE_HOST`, `HOMECARE_PORT`.\\n- Bind loopback by default. There is no authentication; do not expose the port.\\n- On first start create schema and indexes. Schema version 1 is created once; no migration beyond that.\\n- SQLite connection setup: `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON`, `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout=5000`.\\n- Server: `ThreadingHTTPServer` is acceptable, but every write uses one explicit SQLite transaction.\\n- JSON is UTF-8. Maximum request body 1,048,576 bytes. POST and PATCH must send `application/json`; otherwis... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n144:  \"gaps\": [\n145:   \"Upstream status: not_run. The repository was read as evidence only; no build, test, server, TUI, or database was executed, so no upstream behavior is runtime-verified.\",\n146:   \"Runtime verification is not_run for the target too. The probe and architecture are authored artifacts; no server was started and no acceptance case was executed in this task.\",\n147:   \"Single-home and single-user by design; no multi-property, accounts, authentication, sharing, or remote access.\",\n148:   \"No notifications, email, SMS, push, calendar sync, or background scheduler; due work is pull-based through the API and UI.\",\n149:   \"No costs, vendors, receipts, photos, manuals, warranties, projects, quotes, incidents, documents, or LLM features; those upstream surfaces are intentionally out of scope.\",\n150:   \"Every-N-days recurrence differs from upstream interval months; no compatibility with upstream databases, APIs, or schema is claimed.\",\n151:   \"No delete, undo, archive, or restore endpoints; completion history is append-only and test records remain until the disposable data directory is discarded.\",\n152:   \"Validation is strict and date-only; natural-language dates and timezone conversion are unsupported. Server local date can differ by one day from a client in another timezone.\",\n153:   \"The UI is a minimal single-page client, not a polished product; no internationalization, offline cache, or mobile-native behavior.\",\n154:   \"Schema v1 has no migration path. Changing entities later needs an explicit migration or a new disposable database.\",\n155:   \"Concurrency is sized for one user; SQLite WAL and busy_timeout reduce but do not eliminate lock contention.\",\n156:   \"User decision points: confirm one-home scope, the default due date of creation day when no anchor is provided, latest-completion rollover for backdated entries, strict date-only input, and the absence of delete and defect-tracking features.\",\n157:   \"Restart durability may be described as an operator stop and start step in README; it was not run and is not claimed as verified.\"\n158:  ],\n159:  \"repo_name\": \"micasa-dev/micasa\",\n160:  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n161:  \"license_path\": \"LICENSE\"\n162: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/AUTHOR_INPUT.json, lines 1-162\n1: {\n2:  \"name\": \"Home Care Ledger\",\n3:  \"audience\": \"A single homeowner keeping care records for their own home on a local machine, with no accounts, notifications, or multi-property operation.\",\n4:  \"objective\": \"Create the home and its equipment, define every-N-day care plans anchored to them, see exactly which tasks are due or overdue as of a date, record a completion with a note, advance the next due date from the actual completion date, and retrieve care history by home or equipment.\",\n5:  \"workflow\": [\n6:   \"Start the local server against a disposable data directory; initialize the SQLite schema on first start.\",\n7:   \"Create the single home with POST /api/home, then add equipment records with POST /api/equipment anchored by home_id.\",\n8:   \"Create care plans with POST /api/plans using interval_days and an optional equipment anchor.\",\n9:   \"Query GET /api/tasks/due with an explicit as_of and horizon_days to see overdue, due, and upcoming work.\",\n10:   \"Record a completion and note with POST /api/plans/{id}/completions; the same transaction updates the plan next due date.\",\n11:   \"Read GET /api/plans/{id}/completions or GET /api/history filtered by home_id and equipment_id.\",\n12:   \"Use GET / for the basic accessible single-page UI; all actions remain available through the documented JSON API.\"\n13:  ],\n14:  \"acceptance\": [\n15:   \"A fresh database has no home; POST /api/home creates exactly one record with id home, and a second POST returns 409 HOME_EXISTS without mutating the stored home.\",\n16:   \"POST /api/equipment under the existing home returns 201 and round-trips through list and detail; blank names, invalid categories, and unknown homes return 422 or 404 and add no equipment row.\",\n17:   \"POST /api/plans enforces interval_days 1..3650 and mutual exclusion of last_completed_on and first_due_on; GET /api/tasks/due returns exact overdue, due, and upcoming sets at as_of and horizon_days boundaries, while invalid requests write nothing.\",\n18:   \"A completion with note inserts one history row and atomically sets due_on to max(previous last_completed_on, completed_on) plus interval_days; leap-day, month-end, year-end, future-date, oversize-note, and unknown-plan failures leave both plan and completions unchanged.\",\n19:   \"GET /api/history filters by home and equipment and returns documented fields in descending completion order; invalid filters write nothing; GET / is dependency-free accessible HTML and unknown routes or methods return documented JSON errors.\"\n20:  ],\n21:  \"observations\": [\n22:   [\n23:    \"documentation\",\n24:    \"README.md\",\n25:    17,\n26:    17,\n27:    \"Document claim: micasa describes itself as home maintenance from the terminal, a local tool rather than a hosted multi-tenant service.\"\n28:   ],\n29:   [\n30:    \"documentation\",\n31:    \"README.md\",\n32:    25,\n33:    25,\n34:    \"Document claim: the upstream advertises schedules, due dates, and full history.\"\n35:   ],\n36:   [\n37:    \"code_observation\",\n38:    \"internal/data/models.go\",\n39:    104,\n40:    135,\n41:    \"Code observation: HouseProfile stores address, year built, systems, and other attributes; no explicit multi-home ownership table is observed in the selected files.\"\n42:   ],\n43:   [\n44:    \"code_observation\",\n45:    \"internal/data/models.go\",\n46:    201,\n47:    216,\n48:    \"Code observation: Appliance stores make, model, serial, warranty, and location, with no home_id field observed.\"\n49:   ],\n50:   [\n51:    \"code_observation\",\n52:    \"internal/data/models.go\",\n53:    218,\n54:    237,\n55:    \"Code observation: MaintenanceItem has an optional ApplianceID, category, season, interval months, last serviced date, and due date.\"\n56:   ],\n57:   [\n58:    \"code_observation\",\n59:    \"internal/data/models.go\",\n60:    261,\n61:    274,\n62:    \"Code observation: ServiceLogEntry belongs to a maintenance item and stores serviced_at, optional vendor and cost, notes, and timestamps.\"\n63:   ],\n64:   [\n65:    \"code_observation\",\n66:    \"internal/data/store_house.go\",\n67:    22,\n68:    31,\n69:    \"Code observation: CreateHouseProfile counts existing profiles and rejects a second row, implementing one house profile.\"\n70:   ],\n71:   [\n72:    \"code_observation\",\n73:    \"internal/data/store_maintenance.go\",\n74:    24,\n75:    33,\n76:    \"Code observation: ListMaintenanceByAppliance filters maintenance items by appliance id, showing an equipment-anchored query path.\"\n77:   ],\n78:   [\n79:    \"code_observation\",\n80:    \"internal/data/store_servicelog.go\",\n81:    16,\n82:    30,\n83:    \"Code observation: syncLastServiced sets LastServicedAt to the most recent non-deleted serviced_at.\"\n84:   ],\n85:   [\n86:    \"code_observation\",\n87:    \"internal/data/store_servicelog.go\",\n88:    59,\n89:    73,\n90:    \"Code observation: CreateServiceLog runs in a transaction, creates the service log, then syncs the parent maintenance item.\"\n91:   ],\n92:   [\n93:    \"code_observation\",\n94:    \"internal/data/validation.go\",\n95:    168,\n96:    177,\n97:    \"Code observation: ComputeNextDue returns an explicit due date when set, otherwise adds interval months to the last service date.\"\n98:   ],\n99:   [\n100:    \"code_observation\",\n101:    \"internal/data/validation.go\",\n102:    182,\n103:    192,\n104:    \"Code observation: AddMonths clamps the day to the target month end, avoiding the Jan 31 plus one month overflow.\"\n105:   ],\n106:   [\n107:    \"code_observation\",\n108:    \"internal/data/validation.go\",\n109:    98,\n110:    153,\n111:    \"Code observation: interval parsing accepts years and months, not days.\"\n112:   ],\n113:   [\n114:    \"code_observation\",\n115:    \"internal/data/dashboard.go\",\n116:    12,\n117:    25,\n118:    \"Code observation: scheduled maintenance is defined as interval months greater than zero or an explicit due date.\"\n119:   ],\n120:   [\n121:    \"documentation\",\n122:    \"README.md\",\n123:    58,\n124:    58,\n125:    \"Document claim: the upstream is pure Go using SQLite and a terminal UI; this target does not copy or run that implementation.\"\n126:   ]\n127:  ],\n128:  \"inference\": \"Target design inference, not an upstream claim: the pinned research makes the home the subject and requires recurring work plus a durable completion record. Upstream code corroborates that abstract shape but realizes recurrence in months, keeps one house profile, links maintenance to an optional appliance, and does not show an explicit appliance-to-home foreign key in the selected files. The target therefore makes the home anchor explicit through home_id on equipment and plans, uses every-N-days recurrence from the scenario, and keeps only the home, equipment, plan, completion, and history slice. It does not copy upstream code, schema, or UI. Upstream status: not_run; no upstream build, test, server, TUI, or database was started.\",\n129:  \"features\": [\n130:   \"Home and equipment anchor\",\n131:   \"Every-N-day plan and due queue\",\n132:   \"Completion and next-due rollover\",\n133:   \"Anchored care history\",\n134:   \"Accessible localhost UI\"\n135:  ],\n136:  \"goals\": [\n137:   \"In a dedicated data directory, create the single home, add an equipment record under it, and prove duplicate-home and invalid-equipment requests return 409, 422, or 404 without changing stored records.\",\n138:   \"Create plans with interval_days in 1..3650 and verify GET /api/tasks/due returns the exact overdue, due, and upcoming sets at the as_of and horizon_days boundaries while invalid plans write nothing.\",\n139:   \"Record a completion and note in one atomic call and verify due_on becomes max(previous last_completed_on, completed_on) plus interval_days across leap-day, month-end, and year-end examples, with invalid completions leaving no trace.\",\n140:   \"Retrieve completions filtered by home and equipment in documented descending order with plan and equipment names and notes, and reject invalid filters without writes.\",\n141:   \"Load GET / and assert a dependency-free, labelled, keyboard-accessible HTML shell exposes home, equipment, plan, due, completion, and history workflows, while unknown routes and methods return documented JSON errors.\"\n142:  ],\n143:  \"arch\": \"# Home Care Ledger: target architecture\\n\\n## Scope and decisions to confirm\\n- Local single-user target: one homeowner, one home, loopback only.\\n- Python 3.11+ standard library only; SQLite; no third-party packages.\\n- This is a cognition template, not an application and not the upstream micasa codebase.\\n- Deliberately excluded: accounts and authentication, notifications, email, vendors, costs, quotes, projects, documents, manuals, photos, payments, LLM, multi-property, imports and exports, and deletion endpoints.\\n- Decision: exactly one home with fixed id `home`, because the pinned scenario is the user's own home and upstream exposes a single house profile.\\n- Decision: recurrence is every N calendar days, 1..3650, because the scenario says every N days. Upstream uses interval months; this target is not API-compatible with it.\\n- Decision: a plan created without an anchor is due on the server local creation date.\\n- Decision: a backdated completion never moves next due backwards; next due is based on the latest completion date.\\n- Decision: no natural-language dates and no timezone-bearing timestamps in domain dates.\\n\\n## Runtime, data directory, start\\n- Source file `app.py`; database `$HOMECARE_DATA_DIR/homecare.sqlite3`.\\n- `HOMECARE_DATA_DIR` defaults to `./data`; the directory is created if absent.\\n- Start: `python3 app.py --data-dir ./data --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8765`.\\n- Equivalent environment variables: `HOMECARE_DATA_DIR`, `HOMECARE_HOST`, `HOMECARE_PORT`.\\n- Bind loopback by default. There is no authentication; do not expose the port.\\n- On first start create schema and indexes. Schema version 1 is created once; no migration beyond that.\\n- SQLite connection setup: `PRAGMA foreign_keys=ON`, `journal_mode=WAL`, `busy_timeout=5000`.\\n- Server: `ThreadingHTTPServer` is acceptable, but every write uses one explicit SQLite transaction.\\n- JSON is UTF-8. Maximum request body 1,048,576 bytes. POST and PATCH must send `application/json`; otherwis... (line truncated to 2000 chars)\n144:  \"gaps\": [\n145:   \"Upstream status: not_run. The repository was read as evidence only; no build, test, server, TUI, or database was executed, so no upstream behavior is runtime-verified.\",\n146:   \"Runtime verification is not_run for the target too. The probe and architecture are authored artifacts; no server was started and no acceptance case was executed in this task.\",\n147:   \"Single-home and single-user by design; no multi-property, accounts, authentication, sharing, or remote access.\",\n148:   \"No notifications, email, SMS, push, calendar sync, or background scheduler; due work is pull-based through the API and UI.\",\n149:   \"No costs, vendors, receipts, photos, manuals, warranties, projects, quotes, incidents, documents, or LLM features; those upstream surfaces are intentionally out of scope.\",\n150:   \"Every-N-days recurrence differs from upstream interval months; no compatibility with upstream databases, APIs, or schema is claimed.\",\n151:   \"No delete, undo, archive, or restore endpoints; completion history is append-only and test records remain until the disposable data directory is discarded.\",\n152:   \"Validation is strict and date-only; natural-language dates and timezone conversion are unsupported. Server local date can differ by one day from a client in another timezone.\",\n153:   \"The UI is a minimal single-page client, not a polished product; no internationalization, offline cache, or mobile-native behavior.\",\n154:   \"Schema v1 has no migration path. Changing entities later needs an explicit migration or a new disposable database.\",\n155:   \"Concurrency is sized for one user; SQLite WAL and busy_timeout reduce but do not eliminate lock contention.\",\n156:   \"User decision points: confirm one-home scope, the default due date of creation day when no anchor is provided, latest-completion rollover for backdated entries, strict date-only input, and the absence of delete and defect-tracking features.\",\n157:   \"Restart durability may be described as an operator stop and start step in README; it was not run and is not claimed as verified.\"\n158:  ],\n159:  \"repo_name\": \"micasa-dev/micasa\",\n160:  \"license\": \"Apache-2.0\",\n161:  \"license_path\": \"LICENSE\"\n162: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/candidate/AUTHOR_INPUT.json\"}"},"time":{"start":1792571589522,"end":1792571589530}}}}
