{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792571600293,"sessionID":"ses_ea2691a44ffemHBxOiocBq67ci","part":{"partID":"prt_15d97ed14001Z5Du6G1WPUvNEI","sessionID":"ses_ea2691a44ffemHBxOiocBq67ci","messageID":"msg_15d97dde9001G3jNq7jAILvKFp","type":"tool","id":"call_00_8lnbj60n2vommdcv6nnturv8","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/README.md"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/README.md, lines 1-69\n1: <!-- Copyright 2026 Phillip Cloud -->\n2: <!-- Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 -->\n3: \n4: <div align=\"center\">\n5:   <img src=\"images/house.svg\" alt=\"micasa\">\n6: \n7:   <br><br>\n8: \n9:   [![CI](https://github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n10:   [![Release](https://img.shields.io/github/v/release/micasa-dev/micasa)](https://github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/releases/latest)\n11:   [![Go](https://img.shields.io/github/go-mod/go-version/micasa-dev/micasa)](https://go.dev)\n12:   [![Docs](https://img.shields.io/badge/docs-micasa.dev-blue)](https://micasa.dev/docs)\n13: </div>\n14: \n15: # `micasa`\n16: \n17: Home maintenance, from the terminal.\n18: \n19: <div align=\"center\">\n20:   <img src=\"images/demo.webp\" alt=\"micasa demo\" width=\"800\">\n21: </div>\n22: \n23: ## Features\n24: \n25: - **When did I last change the furnace filter?** Schedules, due dates, full history. Set it and forget it.\n26: - **What if we finally did the backyard?** Projects from napkin sketch to completion, or graceful abandonment.\n27: - **How much would it cost to…** Quotes side by side, vendor history, and the math to actually decide.\n28: - **Who did we use last time?** Every contractor, every quote, every job. All searchable.\n29: - **How much have I spent on plumbing this year?** Ask a local LLM. Or don't. Offline until you say otherwise.\n30: \n31: ## Keyboard driven\n32: \n33: Vim-style modal keys: `nav` mode to browse, `edit` mode to change things. Sort by any column, jump to columns with fuzzy search, hide what you don't need, and drill into related records.\n34: \n35: See the full [keybinding reference](https://micasa.dev/docs/reference/keybindings/).\n36: \n37: ## Install\n38: \n39: ```sh\n40: go install github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/cmd/micasa@latest\n41: ```\n42: \n43: Or grab a [binary](https://github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/releases/latest) for Linux, macOS, or Windows.\n44: \n45: Then:\n46: \n47: ```sh\n48: micasa demo         # sample data\n49: micasa              # your house\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ## Documentation\n53: \n54: Full docs at [micasa.dev/docs](https://micasa.dev/docs/).\n55: \n56: ## Development\n57: \n58: [Pure Go](https://go.dev), zero CGO. Built on [Charmbracelet](https://github.com/charmbracelet) + [GORM](https://gorm.io) + [SQLite](https://sqlite.org). TUI design inspired by [VisiData](https://www.visidata.org/). Developed with AI coding agents ([Claude](https://claude.ai), [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)).\n59: \n60: PRs welcome, including AI-assisted ones, as long as you've reviewed and curated the code. See the [contributing guide](https://micasa.dev/docs/development/contributing/).\n61: \n62: ```sh\n63: nix develop                      # enter dev shell\n64: go test -shuffle=on ./...        # run tests\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ## License\n68: \n69: Apache-2.0. See [LICENSE](LICENSE).","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/README.md, lines 1-69\n1: <!-- Copyright 2026 Phillip Cloud -->\n2: <!-- Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0 -->\n3: \n4: <div align=\"center\">\n5:   <img src=\"images/house.svg\" alt=\"micasa\">\n6: \n7:   <br><br>\n8: \n9:   [![CI](https://github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/actions/workflows/ci.yml/badge.svg)](https://github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/actions/workflows/ci.yml)\n10:   [![Release](https://img.shields.io/github/v/release/micasa-dev/micasa)](https://github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/releases/latest)\n11:   [![Go](https://img.shields.io/github/go-mod/go-version/micasa-dev/micasa)](https://go.dev)\n12:   [![Docs](https://img.shields.io/badge/docs-micasa.dev-blue)](https://micasa.dev/docs)\n13: </div>\n14: \n15: # `micasa`\n16: \n17: Home maintenance, from the terminal.\n18: \n19: <div align=\"center\">\n20:   <img src=\"images/demo.webp\" alt=\"micasa demo\" width=\"800\">\n21: </div>\n22: \n23: ## Features\n24: \n25: - **When did I last change the furnace filter?** Schedules, due dates, full history. Set it and forget it.\n26: - **What if we finally did the backyard?** Projects from napkin sketch to completion, or graceful abandonment.\n27: - **How much would it cost to…** Quotes side by side, vendor history, and the math to actually decide.\n28: - **Who did we use last time?** Every contractor, every quote, every job. All searchable.\n29: - **How much have I spent on plumbing this year?** Ask a local LLM. Or don't. Offline until you say otherwise.\n30: \n31: ## Keyboard driven\n32: \n33: Vim-style modal keys: `nav` mode to browse, `edit` mode to change things. Sort by any column, jump to columns with fuzzy search, hide what you don't need, and drill into related records.\n34: \n35: See the full [keybinding reference](https://micasa.dev/docs/reference/keybindings/).\n36: \n37: ## Install\n38: \n39: ```sh\n40: go install github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/cmd/micasa@latest\n41: ```\n42: \n43: Or grab a [binary](https://github.com/micasa-dev/micasa/releases/latest) for Linux, macOS, or Windows.\n44: \n45: Then:\n46: \n47: ```sh\n48: micasa demo         # sample data\n49: micasa              # your house\n50: ```\n51: \n52: ## Documentation\n53: \n54: Full docs at [micasa.dev/docs](https://micasa.dev/docs/).\n55: \n56: ## Development\n57: \n58: [Pure Go](https://go.dev), zero CGO. Built on [Charmbracelet](https://github.com/charmbracelet) + [GORM](https://gorm.io) + [SQLite](https://sqlite.org). TUI design inspired by [VisiData](https://www.visidata.org/). Developed with AI coding agents ([Claude](https://claude.ai), [Claude Code](https://claude.ai/code)).\n59: \n60: PRs welcome, including AI-assisted ones, as long as you've reviewed and curated the code. See the [contributing guide](https://micasa.dev/docs/development/contributing/).\n61: \n62: ```sh\n63: nix develop                      # enter dev shell\n64: go test -shuffle=on ./...        # run tests\n65: ```\n66: \n67: ## License\n68: \n69: Apache-2.0. See [LICENSE](LICENSE)."}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/README.md\"}"},"time":{"start":1792571600148,"end":1792571600293}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1792571600294,"sessionID":"ses_ea2691a44ffemHBxOiocBq67ci","part":{"partID":"prt_15d97ed91001uSwKfdRgV0ISqO","sessionID":"ses_ea2691a44ffemHBxOiocBq67ci","messageID":"msg_15d97dde9001G3jNq7jAILvKFp","type":"tool","id":"call_02_3nb4wd766xzxb7xpyk4pcivd","tool":"read","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"path":"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/internal/data/dashboard.go"},"output":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/internal/data/dashboard.go, lines 1-161\n1: // Copyright 2026 Phillip Cloud\n2: // Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n3: \n4: package data\n5: \n6: import (\n7: \t\"time\"\n8: \n9: \t\"gorm.io/gorm\"\n10: )\n11: \n12: // ListMaintenanceWithSchedule returns all non-deleted maintenance items that\n13: // have a positive interval or an explicit due date, preloading Category and\n14: // Appliance. These are the items eligible for overdue/upcoming computation.\n15: func (s *Store) ListMaintenanceWithSchedule() ([]MaintenanceItem, error) {\n16: \tvar items []MaintenanceItem\n17: \terr := s.db.\n18: \t\tWhere(ColIntervalMonths+\" > 0 OR \"+ColDueDate+\" IS NOT NULL\").\n19: \t\tPreload(\"Category\").\n20: \t\tPreload(\"Appliance\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n21: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n22: \t\t}).\n23: \t\tOrder(ColUpdatedAt + \" desc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n24: \t\tFind(&items).Error\n25: \treturn items, err\n26: }\n27: \n28: // SeasonForMonth returns the season constant for a given calendar month.\n29: // Northern hemisphere: Mar-May spring, Jun-Aug summer, Sep-Nov fall, Dec-Feb winter.\n30: func SeasonForMonth(m time.Month) string {\n31: \tswitch m {\n32: \tcase time.March, time.April, time.May:\n33: \t\treturn SeasonSpring\n34: \tcase time.June, time.July, time.August:\n35: \t\treturn SeasonSummer\n36: \tcase time.September, time.October, time.November:\n37: \t\treturn SeasonFall\n38: \tcase time.December, time.January, time.February:\n39: \t\treturn SeasonWinter\n40: \tdefault:\n41: \t\treturn SeasonWinter\n42: \t}\n43: }\n44: \n45: // ListMaintenanceBySeason returns non-deleted maintenance items tagged with\n46: // the given season, preloading Category and Appliance.\n47: func (s *Store) ListMaintenanceBySeason(season string) ([]MaintenanceItem, error) {\n48: \tvar items []MaintenanceItem\n49: \terr := s.db.\n50: \t\tWhere(ColSeason+\" = ?\", season).\n51: \t\tPreload(\"Category\").\n52: \t\tPreload(\"Appliance\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n53: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n54: \t\t}).\n55: \t\tOrder(ColName + \" asc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n56: \t\tFind(&items).Error\n57: \treturn items, err\n58: }\n59: \n60: // ListActiveProjects returns non-deleted projects with status \"underway\" or\n61: // \"delayed\", preloading ProjectType.\n62: func (s *Store) ListActiveProjects() ([]Project, error) {\n63: \tvar projects []Project\n64: \terr := s.db.\n65: \t\tWhere(ColStatus+\" IN ?\", []string{ProjectStatusInProgress, ProjectStatusDelayed}).\n66: \t\tPreload(\"ProjectType\").\n67: \t\tOrder(ColUpdatedAt + \" desc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n68: \t\tFind(&projects).Error\n69: \treturn projects, err\n70: }\n71: \n72: // ListOpenIncidents returns non-deleted incidents (open or in-progress),\n73: // preloading Appliance and Vendor. Ordered by severity (urgent first) then\n74: // most recently updated.\n75: func (s *Store) ListOpenIncidents() ([]Incident, error) {\n76: \tvar incidents []Incident\n77: \terr := s.db.\n78: \t\tWhere(ColStatus+\" IN ?\", []string{IncidentStatusOpen, IncidentStatusInProgress}).\n79: \t\tPreload(\"Appliance\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n80: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n81: \t\t}).\n82: \t\tPreload(\"Vendor\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n83: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n84: \t\t}).\n85: \t\tOrder(\"CASE \" + ColSeverity +\n86: \t\t\t\" WHEN '\" + IncidentSeverityUrgent + \"' THEN 0\" +\n87: \t\t\t\" WHEN '\" + IncidentSeveritySoon + \"' THEN 1\" +\n88: \t\t\t\" WHEN '\" + IncidentSeverityWhenever + \"' THEN 2\" +\n89: \t\t\t\" ELSE 3 END, \" + ColUpdatedAt + \" desc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n90: \t\tFind(&incidents).Error\n91: \treturn incidents, err\n92: }\n93: \n94: // ListExpiringWarranties returns non-deleted appliances whose warranty expires\n95: // between (now - lookBack) and (now + horizon).\n96: func (s *Store) ListExpiringWarranties(\n97: \tnow time.Time,\n98: \tlookBack, horizon time.Duration,\n99: ) ([]Appliance, error) {\n100: \tvar appliances []Appliance\n101: \tfrom := now.Add(-lookBack)\n102: \tto := now.Add(horizon)\n103: \terr := s.db.\n104: \t\tWhere(ColWarrantyExpiry+\" IS NOT NULL AND \"+ColWarrantyExpiry+\" BETWEEN ? AND ?\", from, to).\n105: \t\tOrder(ColWarrantyExpiry + \" asc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n106: \t\tFind(&appliances).Error\n107: \treturn appliances, err\n108: }\n109: \n110: // ListRecentServiceLogs returns the most recent service log entries across all\n111: // maintenance items, preloading MaintenanceItem and Vendor.\n112: func (s *Store) ListRecentServiceLogs(limit int) ([]ServiceLogEntry, error) {\n113: \tvar entries []ServiceLogEntry\n114: \terr := s.db.\n115: \t\tPreload(\"MaintenanceItem\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n116: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n117: \t\t}).\n118: \t\tPreload(\"Vendor\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n119: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n120: \t\t}).\n121: \t\tOrder(ColServicedAt + \" desc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n122: \t\tLimit(limit).\n123: \t\tFind(&entries).Error\n124: \treturn entries, err\n125: }\n126: \n127: // YTDServiceSpendCents returns the total cost of service log entries with\n128: // ServicedAt on or after the given start-of-year.\n129: func (s *Store) YTDServiceSpendCents(yearStart time.Time) (int64, error) {\n130: \tvar total *int64\n131: \terr := s.db.Model(&ServiceLogEntry{}).\n132: \t\tSelect(\"COALESCE(SUM(\"+ColCostCents+\"), 0)\").\n133: \t\tWhere(ColServicedAt+\" >= ?\", yearStart).\n134: \t\tScan(&total).Error\n135: \tif err != nil {\n136: \t\treturn 0, err\n137: \t}\n138: \tif total == nil {\n139: \t\treturn 0, nil\n140: \t}\n141: \treturn *total, nil\n142: }\n143: \n144: // TotalProjectSpendCents returns the total actual spend across all non-deleted\n145: // projects. Unlike service log entries (which have a serviced_at date),\n146: // projects have no per-transaction date, so YTD filtering is not meaningful.\n147: // The previous updated_at filter was incorrect: editing any project field\n148: // (e.g. description) would cause its spend to appear/disappear from the total.\n149: func (s *Store) TotalProjectSpendCents() (int64, error) {\n150: \tvar total *int64\n151: \terr := s.db.Model(&Project{}).\n152: \t\tSelect(\"COALESCE(SUM(\" + ColActualCents + \"), 0)\").\n153: \t\tScan(&total).Error\n154: \tif err != nil {\n155: \t\treturn 0, err\n156: \t}\n157: \tif total == nil {\n158: \t\treturn 0, nil\n159: \t}\n160: \treturn *total, nil\n161: }","title":"read","metadata":{"metadata":{"truncated":false},"content":[{"type":"text","text":"Read file /Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/internal/data/dashboard.go, lines 1-161\n1: // Copyright 2026 Phillip Cloud\n2: // Licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0\n3: \n4: package data\n5: \n6: import (\n7: \t\"time\"\n8: \n9: \t\"gorm.io/gorm\"\n10: )\n11: \n12: // ListMaintenanceWithSchedule returns all non-deleted maintenance items that\n13: // have a positive interval or an explicit due date, preloading Category and\n14: // Appliance. These are the items eligible for overdue/upcoming computation.\n15: func (s *Store) ListMaintenanceWithSchedule() ([]MaintenanceItem, error) {\n16: \tvar items []MaintenanceItem\n17: \terr := s.db.\n18: \t\tWhere(ColIntervalMonths+\" > 0 OR \"+ColDueDate+\" IS NOT NULL\").\n19: \t\tPreload(\"Category\").\n20: \t\tPreload(\"Appliance\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n21: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n22: \t\t}).\n23: \t\tOrder(ColUpdatedAt + \" desc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n24: \t\tFind(&items).Error\n25: \treturn items, err\n26: }\n27: \n28: // SeasonForMonth returns the season constant for a given calendar month.\n29: // Northern hemisphere: Mar-May spring, Jun-Aug summer, Sep-Nov fall, Dec-Feb winter.\n30: func SeasonForMonth(m time.Month) string {\n31: \tswitch m {\n32: \tcase time.March, time.April, time.May:\n33: \t\treturn SeasonSpring\n34: \tcase time.June, time.July, time.August:\n35: \t\treturn SeasonSummer\n36: \tcase time.September, time.October, time.November:\n37: \t\treturn SeasonFall\n38: \tcase time.December, time.January, time.February:\n39: \t\treturn SeasonWinter\n40: \tdefault:\n41: \t\treturn SeasonWinter\n42: \t}\n43: }\n44: \n45: // ListMaintenanceBySeason returns non-deleted maintenance items tagged with\n46: // the given season, preloading Category and Appliance.\n47: func (s *Store) ListMaintenanceBySeason(season string) ([]MaintenanceItem, error) {\n48: \tvar items []MaintenanceItem\n49: \terr := s.db.\n50: \t\tWhere(ColSeason+\" = ?\", season).\n51: \t\tPreload(\"Category\").\n52: \t\tPreload(\"Appliance\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n53: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n54: \t\t}).\n55: \t\tOrder(ColName + \" asc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n56: \t\tFind(&items).Error\n57: \treturn items, err\n58: }\n59: \n60: // ListActiveProjects returns non-deleted projects with status \"underway\" or\n61: // \"delayed\", preloading ProjectType.\n62: func (s *Store) ListActiveProjects() ([]Project, error) {\n63: \tvar projects []Project\n64: \terr := s.db.\n65: \t\tWhere(ColStatus+\" IN ?\", []string{ProjectStatusInProgress, ProjectStatusDelayed}).\n66: \t\tPreload(\"ProjectType\").\n67: \t\tOrder(ColUpdatedAt + \" desc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n68: \t\tFind(&projects).Error\n69: \treturn projects, err\n70: }\n71: \n72: // ListOpenIncidents returns non-deleted incidents (open or in-progress),\n73: // preloading Appliance and Vendor. Ordered by severity (urgent first) then\n74: // most recently updated.\n75: func (s *Store) ListOpenIncidents() ([]Incident, error) {\n76: \tvar incidents []Incident\n77: \terr := s.db.\n78: \t\tWhere(ColStatus+\" IN ?\", []string{IncidentStatusOpen, IncidentStatusInProgress}).\n79: \t\tPreload(\"Appliance\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n80: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n81: \t\t}).\n82: \t\tPreload(\"Vendor\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n83: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n84: \t\t}).\n85: \t\tOrder(\"CASE \" + ColSeverity +\n86: \t\t\t\" WHEN '\" + IncidentSeverityUrgent + \"' THEN 0\" +\n87: \t\t\t\" WHEN '\" + IncidentSeveritySoon + \"' THEN 1\" +\n88: \t\t\t\" WHEN '\" + IncidentSeverityWhenever + \"' THEN 2\" +\n89: \t\t\t\" ELSE 3 END, \" + ColUpdatedAt + \" desc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n90: \t\tFind(&incidents).Error\n91: \treturn incidents, err\n92: }\n93: \n94: // ListExpiringWarranties returns non-deleted appliances whose warranty expires\n95: // between (now - lookBack) and (now + horizon).\n96: func (s *Store) ListExpiringWarranties(\n97: \tnow time.Time,\n98: \tlookBack, horizon time.Duration,\n99: ) ([]Appliance, error) {\n100: \tvar appliances []Appliance\n101: \tfrom := now.Add(-lookBack)\n102: \tto := now.Add(horizon)\n103: \terr := s.db.\n104: \t\tWhere(ColWarrantyExpiry+\" IS NOT NULL AND \"+ColWarrantyExpiry+\" BETWEEN ? AND ?\", from, to).\n105: \t\tOrder(ColWarrantyExpiry + \" asc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n106: \t\tFind(&appliances).Error\n107: \treturn appliances, err\n108: }\n109: \n110: // ListRecentServiceLogs returns the most recent service log entries across all\n111: // maintenance items, preloading MaintenanceItem and Vendor.\n112: func (s *Store) ListRecentServiceLogs(limit int) ([]ServiceLogEntry, error) {\n113: \tvar entries []ServiceLogEntry\n114: \terr := s.db.\n115: \t\tPreload(\"MaintenanceItem\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n116: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n117: \t\t}).\n118: \t\tPreload(\"Vendor\", func(q *gorm.DB) *gorm.DB {\n119: \t\t\treturn q.Unscoped()\n120: \t\t}).\n121: \t\tOrder(ColServicedAt + \" desc, \" + ColID + \" desc\").\n122: \t\tLimit(limit).\n123: \t\tFind(&entries).Error\n124: \treturn entries, err\n125: }\n126: \n127: // YTDServiceSpendCents returns the total cost of service log entries with\n128: // ServicedAt on or after the given start-of-year.\n129: func (s *Store) YTDServiceSpendCents(yearStart time.Time) (int64, error) {\n130: \tvar total *int64\n131: \terr := s.db.Model(&ServiceLogEntry{}).\n132: \t\tSelect(\"COALESCE(SUM(\"+ColCostCents+\"), 0)\").\n133: \t\tWhere(ColServicedAt+\" >= ?\", yearStart).\n134: \t\tScan(&total).Error\n135: \tif err != nil {\n136: \t\treturn 0, err\n137: \t}\n138: \tif total == nil {\n139: \t\treturn 0, nil\n140: \t}\n141: \treturn *total, nil\n142: }\n143: \n144: // TotalProjectSpendCents returns the total actual spend across all non-deleted\n145: // projects. Unlike service log entries (which have a serviced_at date),\n146: // projects have no per-transaction date, so YTD filtering is not meaningful.\n147: // The previous updated_at filter was incorrect: editing any project field\n148: // (e.g. description) would cause its spend to appear/disappear from the total.\n149: func (s *Store) TotalProjectSpendCents() (int64, error) {\n150: \tvar total *int64\n151: \terr := s.db.Model(&Project{}).\n152: \t\tSelect(\"COALESCE(SUM(\" + ColActualCents + \"), 0)\").\n153: \t\tScan(&total).Error\n154: \tif err != nil {\n155: \t\treturn 0, err\n156: \t}\n157: \tif total == nil {\n158: \t\treturn 0, nil\n159: \t}\n160: \treturn *total, nil\n161: }"}],"providerCall":{"executed":false},"providerResult":{"executed":false},"rawInput":"{\"path\": \"/Users/milin/2026/软件开发/application-atlas/docs/template-factory/go-auxiliary-pilot-2026-10-21/home-care/calls/blueprint-spec-review-aux/source/upstream/internal/data/dashboard.go\"}"},"time":