{"type":"text","timestamp":1792571890088,"sessionID":"ses_ea2691a44ffemHBxOiocBq67ci","part":{"id":"prt_15d9c4af4002tDXQo5baumr75t","sessionID":"ses_ea2691a44ffemHBxOiocBq67ci","messageID":"msg_15d9b44b5001vnZnbCVTzbwoPi","type":"text","text":"{\"input_digest\":\"db3971272dea6ada40ff45ca8d4871f9ca719189917eecace4561122e1b7c20a\",\"verdict\":\"pass\",\"checks\":{\"leaf_scope\":true,\"source_fidelity\":true,\"design_distinction\":true,\"core_journey\":true,\"architecture\":true,\"acceptance\":true,\"limits_and_safety\":true},\"observations\":[{\"index\":0,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"README.md:17 states 'Home maintenance, from the terminal'; the local install/run instructions at README.md:37-50 support the local-tool characterization, and the observation does not claim a hosted multi-tenant service is described in that line.\"},{\"index\":1,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"README.md:25 says exactly 'Schedules, due dates, full history,' matching the observation.\"},{\"index\":2,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"models.go:104-135 defines HouseProfile with address fields at lines 107-111, YearBuilt at 112, and system fields at 117-126; no HomeID or ownership table appears in the selected files.\"},{\"index\":3,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"models.go:201-216 defines Appliance with Brand (make), ModelNumber, SerialNumber, WarrantyExpiry, and Location; no home_id field is present.\"},{\"index\":4,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"models.go:218-237 defines MaintenanceItem with optional *ApplianceID at line 223, CategoryID at 221, Season at 225, IntervalMonths at 227, LastServicedAt at 226, and DueDate at 228.\"},{\"index\":5,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"models.go:261-274 defines ServiceLogEntry with MaintenanceItemID at 263, ServicedAt at 265, optional VendorID at 266, CostCents at 268, Notes at 269, and CreatedAt/UpdatedAt at 271-272.\"},{\"index\":6,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"store_house.go:22-31 counts HouseProfile rows and returns an error when count > 0, so a second profile is rejected.\"},{\"index\":7,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"store_maintenance.go:24-33 filters on ApplianceID via Where(ColApplianceID + ' = ?', applianceID), confirming an equipment-anchored query path.\"},{\"index\":8,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"store_servicelog.go:16-30 orders by ServicedAt descending and updates LastServicedAt to the first latest non-deleted entry; it leaves the field unchanged only when no entries exist.\"},{\"index\":9,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"store_servicelog.go:59-73 wraps creation and syncLastServiced in s.db.Transaction, creating the service log before syncing the parent maintenance item.\"},{\"index\":10,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"validation.go:168-177 returns DueDate immediately when non-nil, then uses AddMonths(last, intervalMonths) when last exists and intervalMonths > 0; the summary is accurate for recurring scheduled items, with the nil/non-positive guard visible in the cited range.\"},{\"index\":11,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"validation.go:182-192 computes the target month's last day and clamps the day to it before constructing the date, preventing the Jan 31 plus one month overflow.\"},{\"index\":12,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"validation.go:98-153's intervalRe and ParseIntervalMonths accept year and month suffixes and bare integers interpreted as months; no day unit is accepted.\"},{\"index\":13,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"dashboard.go:12-25 filters with interval_months > 0 OR due_date IS NOT NULL, matching the stated definition of scheduled maintenance.\"},{\"index\":14,\"verdict\":\"accepted\",\"reason\":\"README.md:58 states Pure Go, zero CGO, GORM plus SQLite, and a TUI; the no-copy/no-run sentence is the candidate's own boundary and is repeated in the gaps without claiming upstream execution.\"}],\"issues\":[],\"summary\":\"The pinned source citations align with the actual files. The candidate stays within the home plus recurring-care plus completion-history scope, keeps target decisions separate from upstream facts, and covers the end-to-end home/equipment/plan/due/completion/rollover/history journey. The architecture and acceptance probe specify the API, error codes, date-only rules, atomic completion updates, and zero-write negative checks, including leap-day, month-end, year-end, future-date, oversize-note, and unknown-plan cases. Limits explicitly state that neither upstream nor target was run and that no certification is claimed.\"}","time":{"start":1792571886324,"end":1792571890088}}}
